WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.280
- Well, I can't help, but notice

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.310
that in SWAT and in Criminal Minds

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.678
your character loves to kick in doors.

00:00:06.678 --> 00:00:08.450
(laughing)

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.650
And I just need, before
you even talk about it,

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.030
I need you to know that I
have kicked in the door.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:13.863
- Oh, have you?

00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:15.740
- I have kicked in a
door that a contractor

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.530
had to come to our house
and replace the door.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.363
- Okay.

00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:21.990
- Because the first time I was,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.930
whenever I was with my ex
and it was the first time

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.578
I was watching his
children and we were dating

00:00:26.578 --> 00:00:29.227
and I got locked in my bathroom.

00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:30.071
(laughing)

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:31.474
And I was like, what?

00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:32.307
- Did he lock you in the bathroom?

00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:33.420
How, no, he was gone.
(laughing)

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.140
It was my first time
like taking care of them

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.248
and I was freaking out 'cause I was like,

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:38.545
this is not happening on my watch.

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:41.350
I literally kicked the door down in,

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.827
in my bathroom in my house.

00:00:42.827 --> 00:00:43.660
- Isn't that a good feeling though?

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.883
- You know what,
- Isn't it, come on.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:45.870
- You know what I gotta tell you,

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.510
if you can afford it, try it.
(laughing)

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.140
Like you saying, it felt really good

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.190
and, and it also like,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.700
it was funny 'cause
the contractor is like,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.987
you're allowed to watch
my children any time

00:00:57.987 --> 00:00:58.820
(laughing)

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.611
'cause I was like, this is
not happening on my watch,

00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:04.490
but it does, it feels so powerful.

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:05.323
- Oh yeah, no
- Yes.

00:01:05.323 --> 00:01:07.630
- I mean on my last show, Criminal Minds,

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.463
- Yeah.

00:01:08.463 --> 00:01:10.570
- Derek Morgan, there was a stint

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.290
where 'cause the first
season they had me in suits

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.123
and like just--

00:01:14.123 --> 00:01:14.985
- Oh that would be hard.

00:01:14.985 --> 00:01:16.839
- They had like grandpa clothes

00:01:16.839 --> 00:01:17.672
- Yeah.
- And I was like,

00:01:17.672 --> 00:01:18.505
yo, I'm athletic.
- Yeah.

00:01:18.505 --> 00:01:19.338
- You know, put me in the jeans

00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:21.350
and the t-shirt I'm physical.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.183
And so once they figured it out

00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:23.360
and took a chance that
I could run and jump

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.700
and do this stuff, all of a sudden I was,

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.210
it seemed like every other episode,

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.300
I was either tackling
somebody for no reason,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.900
- Yeah.
- or I was kicking down doors.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.910
They actually gave me a nickname,

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:33.410
captain kicked door down,

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.580
captain kicked door down guy.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.760
(laughing)

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:37.593
- That's a long one.

00:01:37.593 --> 00:01:39.040
- So every episode I was like, FBI!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.600
And slam through a door

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.070
and what was funny is every time

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.430
we would kick through the door,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.640
then I'd go, FBI!

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.565
And the next word out of
my mouth would be, clear.

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:48.180
'Cause we were always late.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.013
They were always gone.

00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:49.846
They're already gone.

00:01:49.846 --> 00:01:52.030
So I already did the tough guy stuff,

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.370
but there was nothing there.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.760
- No, I love that though.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.110
That seems like such a fun job

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:56.972
and it seems like such a fun team

00:01:56.972 --> 00:01:57.805
- Oh we had a ball.
- y'all hang out

00:01:57.805 --> 00:01:59.810
off the set too, that's so cool.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:00.643
- Just, I mean,

00:02:00.643 --> 00:02:01.476
I don't think there's a lot of shows

00:02:01.476 --> 00:02:02.470
like ours on television.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.500
I, you know, I'm biased, but,

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.693
but what is the motto when SWAT,

00:02:04.693 --> 00:02:07.338
we help those who can't
help them, we help those

00:02:07.338 --> 00:02:09.060
who can't help themselves.
- Help themselves.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.765
- SWAT is not about kicking
ass, it's about saving lives.

00:02:11.765 --> 00:02:12.690
- Yeah, I love that.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.490
- Street, street, street!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.323
(laughing)

00:02:15.323 --> 00:02:16.156
Never be in a hurry to die!

00:02:16.156 --> 00:02:18.257
- You got tough all of a sudden.

